-- title:
--   Degree bound over L(j(q^N)) at level Γ_H(N²M')
-- statement:
--   Fix positive integers $N$ and $M'$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/N^2M')^\times$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (N ^ 2 * M') H)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!) \to L(\!(q)\!)$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ` attached to the subgroup $\Gamma_H(N^2M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, namely the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N^2M')$ whose lower right entry reduces into $H$. Assume given $j \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}\sum_n a_n q^n$, the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, and $y \in K$ whose expansion is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L N`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the same series with coefficients in $L$ and with $q$ replaced by $q^N$. The conclusion is that $K$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $L(y)$ generated by $y$, and that $[K : L(y)]$ is at most the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_H(N^2M')$ together with $-1$.
--
--   This is the upper bound for the degree of the level $\Gamma_H(N^2M')$ $q$-expansion function field over the subfield generated by $j(q^N)$, with the bound given by the index of $\pm\Gamma_H(N^2M')$; it is the general-$H$ form of the classical degree computation for the modular equation of level $N$. It feeds the density statement for the classifying map used in the Diamond-style argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_finiteDimensional_and_finrank_adjoin_le_index_of_coe_eq_jqNModC_of_eq_laurentBaseChange_gammaH.lean

